.TH DEOPJUFY-VIEW 1 "2026-08-21" "deopjufy 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deopjufy-view \- browse recovered OPJ and OPJU content through the deopjufy CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deopjufy-view
.RI [ FILE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B deopjufy-view
is an optional read-only wxPython client for
.BR deopjufy (1).
It does not import parser internals. Project discovery invokes
.BR "deopjufy list --json" ;
activating an object invokes
.BR "deopjufy get --json" .
Whole-project export invokes
.BR "deopjufy extract" .
.PP
Several OPJ or OPJU projects may be opened in one process. Catalogs are loaded
with a bounded worker pool. Retrieved objects are cached in memory by document
digest and item ID for the lifetime of the process.
.PP
The viewer is a recovery browser, not an Origin replacement. It cannot edit
projects, execute scripts, render graph definitions, reconstruct undecoded graph
styling, or broaden the parser's partial format coverage.
.SH DISCLAIMER
This software is vibe-coded, use it carefully for one-off tasks.
.SH INTERFACE
The window contains a compact action bar, a path-derived Project Explorer on the
left, a tabbed document area on the right, and a status bar. There is no permanent
diagnostics or property panel.
.PP
Catalog hierarchy follows exact
.B source_object_path
components. The viewer does not invent type buckets that are absent from parser
evidence. Native icons distinguish projects, workbooks, worksheets, graphs,
notes, functions, media, and recovery evidence.
.PP
Recovery-only, heuristic, raw, parser-boundary, and unknown leaves are hidden by
default. Use
.B View -> Show unknown/recovery evidence
to expose them. Expand, collapse, and single-child-group unwrapping commands are
available from the View menu.
.SH VIEWS
.SS Tables
Worksheets sharing one exact workbook path open as one document with explicit
sheet controls. Tables use a virtual grid, so scrolling does not start new CLI
processes. Recovered long names, units, comments, formulas, types, and X/Y roles
appear as frozen metadata rows when available.
.PP
The grid provides numeric alignment, clipped cell boundaries, row labels,
keyboard navigation, selection, copying, and rendered-text column sizing.
.SS Images and graph previews
Recovered images and parser-linked stored graph previews use a fit-to-window
image view. The viewer displays a plot only when the named catalog page has an
exact stored-preview link. It does not synthesize a plot from a partial graph
definition.
.SS Notes and structured metadata
Notes use read-only text views. Graph metadata and other structured retrieval
payloads use formatted text. Properties are displayed as labeled fields rather
than a raw JSON dump. Parser warnings are available from
.BR "View -> Diagnostics" .
.SH EXPORT
.SS Current item
.B Export
can save the complete retrieval response, the recovered primary artifact,
CSV/TSV/JSONL/XLSX tables, exact images or stored previews, and selected grid
cells as CSV or TSV. The tree context menu exposes the same applicable actions.
.SS Complete project
.B Export All
invokes the canonical extraction command. It offers readable CSV, readable XLSX,
or complete recovery with an exact byte map. A new project-named directory is
created below the selected destination. The viewer never requests
.B --force
and therefore does not overwrite an existing export.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TS
tab(|);
l lw(42n).
Key|Action
Ctrl+O|Open one or more projects
Ctrl+F|Search the project tree
Enter or Space|Open the selected tree item
Shift+F10|Open the tree context menu
Ctrl+S|Export the current item
Ctrl+Shift+S|Export all from the active project
Ctrl+C|Copy selected cells
Ctrl+W|Close the current workbook or item tab
Ctrl+Tab|Select the next document or workbook
Ctrl+PageUp/PageDown|Select the previous or next sheet
F6|Switch between project tree and document
Ctrl+Shift+E|Expand all project branches
Ctrl+Shift+C|Collapse all project branches
Alt+Enter|Show properties
+, -, or 0|Zoom in, zoom out, or fit preview
F1|Show the complete keyboard reference
.TE
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Install the optional viewer dependencies with:
.EX
uv sync --extra viewer
.EE
.PP
The viewer requires wxPython. XLSX export uses openpyxl. Neither dependency is
imported by the base CLI path.
.SH STATE AND FILES
The viewer creates no application configuration, persistent cache, recent-file
list, window-state file, or project database. It makes no hidden network calls.
Process-local caches disappear on exit. Temporary lazy-retrieval files use a
cleaned system temporary directory.
.PP
The only persistent output is a path explicitly selected by the user. This
stateless behavior is compatible with the XDG base-directory convention because
no state directory is required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 5
wxPython is unavailable.
